  "live_records": {
    "q-71569": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71569",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2},$ find the equation of the level surface $f(x,y,z)=9.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=9.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface for $c=9$ is the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
