    "q-129188": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129188",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{z}-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},$ find the equation of the level surface $f(x,y,z)=4.$",
      "worked_solution": "The level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {e}^{z}-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {e}^{z} & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4 \\\\ z & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface for $c=4$ is the surface $z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
