    "q-71570": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71570",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y,z)=12{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2},$ find the equation of the level surface $f(x,y,z)=12.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=12.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ 12{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}-{z}^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface for $c=12$ is the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}-{z}^{2}=-1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
