    "q-129203": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129203",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡z?$",
      "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡z & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡z & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-c \\\\ z & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get a family of curves:\n\n$$\nz={e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-c},\\,c\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
