    "q-71595": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71595",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)-\\sqrt{xy}$ that passes through the point $P(1,1,e).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1,e) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1\\cdot 1\\cdot e)-\\sqrt{1\\cdot 1}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=0.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)-\\sqrt{xy} & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz) & =\\sqrt{xy} \\\\ xyz & ={e}^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\ z & =\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(1,1,e)$ is the surface $z=\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{xy}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-71595-a",
