    "q-129190": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129190",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=x-2y+z$ that passes through the point $P(1,1,-1).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1,-1) & =1-2(1)+(-1) \\\\  & =1-2-1 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=-2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ x-2y+z & =-2 \\\\ x-2y+z+2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(1,1,-1)$ is the plane $x-2y+z+2=0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-129190-a",
