    "q-129191": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129191",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{z}{y-x}$ that passes through the point $P(2,1,3).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,1,3) & =\\frac{z}{y-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1-2} \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=-3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\frac{z}{y-x} & =-3 \\\\ z & =-3(y-x) \\\\ z & =3x-3y \\\\ 3x-3y-z & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(2,1,3)$ is the plane $3x-3y-z=0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-129191-a",
